## Overview

`Cyrena.Extensa.Components` is the Blazor UI library for the Extensa extension marketplace. It provides components for browsing, downloading, installing, and managing extensions from remote plugin servers. Includes a background download service with progress reporting.

**Assembly**: `Cyrena.Extensa.Components`  
**Namespaces**: `Cyrena.Extensa.Components`, `Cyrena.Extensa.Components.Pages`, `Cyrena.Extensa.Components.Shared`, `Cyrena.Extensa.Contracts`, `Cyrena.Extensa.Models`, `Cyrena.Extensa.Options`, `Cyrena.Extensa.Services`, `Cyrena.Extensions`

---

## Contracts

### `IPackageManager`
Manages the package index and download queue.

```csharp
public interface IPackageManager
{
    bool IsIndexing { get; }
    bool IsDownloading { get; }
    PackageManagerStatus Status { get; }
    IReadOnlyList<Exception> Errors { get; }
    IReadOnlyList<QueuedDownload> Downloads { get; }

    Task IndexPackagesAsync(CancellationToken ct = default);
    Task<IReadOnlyList<Package>> ListPackagesAsync(CancellationToken ct = default);
    Task<Package?> GetPackageAsync(string packageId, CancellationToken ct = default);

    void EnqueueDownload(PluginServer server, string packageId, Version version);
    void EnqueueDownload(Package package);
    Task EnqueueDownloadAsync(Package package, CancellationToken ct = default);
    bool IsQueued(string packageId);
    QueuedDownload? GetNextDownload();
    void ReportCurrentDownloadProgress(QueuedDownload? downoad, double progress);
    void ClearErrors();
}
```

**Known issues:**
- `ReportCurrentDownloadProgress` parameter `downoad` is misspelled (should be `download`)
- `IsQueued()` checks `_current?.PackageId` but `_current` is never set in `PackageManager` (dead code)
- `EnqueueDownload` has two overloads with inconsistent signatures

### `IPluginPackageService`
Queries and downloads packages from plugin servers.

```csharp
public interface IPluginPackageService
{
    Task<IReadOnlyList<Package>> GetPackagesAsync(PluginServer server, CancellationToken ct = default);
    Task<Package?> GetPackageAsync(PluginServer server, string packageId, CancellationToken ct = default);
    Task<PackageSearchResult> SearchPackagesAsync(string applicationId, string query, CancellationToken ct = default);
    Task<PackageDownloadResult> DownloadPackageAsync(PluginServer server, string packageId, Version? version, IProgress<double>? progress, CancellationToken ct = default);
}
```

**Known issues:**
- `SearchPackagesAsync` takes `applicationId` but ignores it — searches all enabled servers
- Creates new `HttpClient` per request (socket exhaustion risk)
- `PackageListResponse` extends `List<Package>` unnecessarily

### `IPluginServerService`
Manages plugin server configuration.

```csharp
public interface IPluginServerService
{
    event EventHandler<IReadOnlyList<PluginServer>>? ServersChanged;
    Task<IReadOnlyList<PluginServer>> GetAllServers();
    Task<IReadOnlyList<PluginServer>> GetEnabledServers();
    Task<PluginServer?> GetServer(string serverId);
    Task AddServerAsync(PluginServer server);
    Task<PluginServer?> UpdateServerAsync(PluginServer server);
    Task RemoveServerAsync(PluginServer server);
}
```

**Known issues:**
- `GetAllServers()`, `GetEnabledServers()`, `GetServer()` lack `CancellationToken` parameters
- Merges persisted and default servers on every call (no caching)
- Default servers don't consistently set `IsDefault = true`

